<title>USA: Vivus tests of impotence products positive.</title>
<headline>Vivus tests of impotence products positive.</headline>
<dateline>MENLO PARK, Calif. 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>VIVUS Inc said Monday it had achieved positive results from clinical studies of two new products for the treatment of erectile dysfunction, commonly known as impotence.</p>
<p>In a double-blind, multi-center trial of 415 patients with chronic erectile dysfunction, designed to evaluate the benefit of adding prazosin to transurethral therapy with alprostadil, six of nine combinations resulted in statistically significant higher rates of intercourse, compared to alprostadil alone.</p>
</text>
